## Installation

### Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/AI-Recruitment-Copilot.git

cd AI-Recruitment-Copilot
```

---

## Backend Setup

Navigate to backend

```bash
cd backend
```

Create virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate

### Windows

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### Linux/Mac

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Configure Environment

Create a `.env` file.

Example:

```env
DATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://root:password@localhost/recruitment_copilot
```

Replace the password with your MySQL password.

---

## Run Backend

```bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Backend will run at

```
http://localhost:8000
```

Swagger Documentation

```
http://localhost:8000/docs
```

---

## Frontend Setup

Navigate to frontend

```bash
cd frontend
```

If using the HTML/CSS version, simply open `index.html` with Live Server or any local web server.

If using the Vite version:

```bash
npm install

npm run dev
```

---

## API Endpoints

### Resume

```
POST /upload
```

Upload a resume.

---

### Candidates

```
GET /candidates
```

Retrieve all candidates.

```
GET /candidate/{id}
```

Retrieve candidate details.

```
DELETE /candidate/{id}
```

Delete a candidate.

---

### Dashboard

```
GET /dashboard/stats
```

Retrieve dashboard statistics.

---

### Analytics

```
GET /analytics
```

Retrieve analytics data.

---

## Workflow

1. Upload resume
2. Resume parser extracts information
3. Candidate data is stored in MySQL
4. Dashboard displays recruitment statistics
5. Analytics visualizes candidate insights
6. Recruiters can search and manage candidates

